„­bible_version£KJV¤book'§chapter¨sections…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|And when they drew nigh unto Jerusalem, and were come to Bethphage, unto the mount of Olives, then sent Jesus two disciples,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›saying unto them, Go into the village over against you, and straightway ye shall find an ass tied, and a colt with her: loose them, and bring them unto me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoAnd if any man say ought unto you, ye shall say, The Lord hath need of them; and straightway he will send them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVAll this was done, that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤text½Tell ye the daughter of Sion,¦layout ‚¤textÙ"Behold, thy King cometh unto thee,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¾Meek, and sitting upon an ass,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¾And a colt the foal of an ass.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8And the disciples went, and did as Jesus commanded them,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[and brought the ass, and the colt, and put on them their clothes, and they set him thereon.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚And a very great multitude spread their garments in the way; others cut down branches from the trees, and strawed them in the way.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®And the multitudes that went before, and that followed, cried, saying, Hosanna to the son of David: Blessed is he that cometh in the name of the Lord; Hosanna in the highest.¦layout ªlast_verse	…¤book'§chapter«first_verse
